# Third-party clones — DO NOT vendor. Re-clone via reports/p0_triage.md §2.
external/

# Build / JIT caches and SLURM job logs (T5 harness)
**/.torch_ext/
**/.triton_cache/
**/.triton_cache*/
*.out
*.err
*.zip

# Python bytecode — root ignores these but `!**/results/**` re-includes under
# results/; re-ignore here (deeper file wins) so analysis-script caches stay out.
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# (root .gitignore already ignores *.json, *.log, *.png, __pycache__, *.so)

# P1.4 temp markers
.nh_decode_sm_*
*.jid
.*_jid

# P1.4-1.6 runtime scratch: per-job decode-SM mode files + bench per-request dumps
.*_mode_*
.p17mode_*
.zbpx_*
.la_chk_*
*.jsonl
*.log

# keep engine-port env docs (root .gitignore ignores env/)
!env/
!env/**

# p1_gates raw-dump policy (2026-08-06): raw serving artifacts follow the
# project-wide "harness + verdict tracked, raw not" convention above (the
# blanket *.jsonl/*.log/*.out/*.err rules already cover gate1's telemetry
# dumps, bench_serving JSONL, and SLURM stdout/stderr, and **/.triton_cache*/
# already covers the per-job Triton caches — see gate1_run.sbatch's own
# "same scope discipline as m3r2_pinforce.sbatch" note). Two narrow
# exceptions are carved back in because they are evidentiary, not raw: the
# Gate 1 server logs are cited by line number in reports/CONSENSUS.md
# (`gate1_srv_874478.log:32` is the partition-table citation), and the
# verify/ logs are the reproduction output substantiating the rev13 P1
# bootstrap-CI coverage correction — both are small, human-authored-scale
# outputs, not multi-MB per-request telemetry.
!results/p1_gates/gate1/gate1_srv_*.log
!results/p1_gates/verify/*.log

# Gate 2 (HOLB-probe 4-arm) raw-dump policy (2026-08-07), extending the
# 2026-08-06 gate1 policy above to gate2. Same "harness + verdict tracked,
# raw not" rule, evaluated file-by-file:
#   - report/result/correctness json + txt: tracked — these ARE the G3/G4/G5
#     verdict artifacts (g2_holb_analyze.py's scored output).
#   - flags_*.json (`/get_server_info` realized-vs-target dumps, PREREG_GATE2
#     section 1.2): tracked — this is the only record of the flags gate, no
#     other file substitutes for it, and it is small (~20KB/file).
#   - prompt_*.txt / prompt_meta_*.json: tracked — provenance for exactly
#     which prompt produced the G3 sha256 (small, human-scale).
#   - manifest_diff_holb_*.txt / runtime_source_manifest_holb_*.sha256:
#     tracked — same convention as the shared sync manifest above.
#   - *.raw.json (the raw HTTP call1/call2 responses behind the G3 sha256):
#     NOT tracked. The sha256 + PASS/FAIL is already recorded in
#     *_correctness_*.json; the raw response body is an intermediate
#     scratch artifact, not cited by line number anywhere, and reproducing
#     it means re-running the arm, not diffing a stored blob.
#   - *_srv_*.log: already excluded by the blanket *.log rule above (no
#     citation-by-line-number found in gate2 docs as of 2026-08-07, so no
#     exception carved back — contrast gate1's gate1_srv_*.log, which IS
#     cited). *.holb.jsonl / windows_*.jsonl / bench *.jsonl and
#     .triton_cache_*/ are likewise already excluded by existing rules
#     above; verified, no new rule needed for those.
!results/p1_gates/gate2/*_flags_*.json
!results/p1_gates/gate2/*_report_*.json
!results/p1_gates/gate2/*_correctness_*.json
results/p1_gates/gate2/*.raw.json

# G2CTRL / E-A raw-dump policy (2026-08-08), extending the 2026-08-06/07 gate2
# policy above to the reproducibility-control campaign (g2ctrl_*, jobs
# 875610/875611) and the mixed-chunk-lever campaign (g2ea_*/g2eaprobe_*, jobs
# 875654/875657/875661). Checked file-by-file against the untracked set (421
# files as of 2026-08-08) before writing anything below:
#   - *.holb.jsonl / bench *.jsonl / *_srv_*.log / .triton_cache_{ea,probe,g2ctrl}_*/
#     are ALREADY excluded by the extension-based rules above (*.jsonl, *.log,
#     **/.triton_cache*/ match by suffix, not job-prefix) — confirmed none of
#     these leaked into `git status` as untracked for the new naming.
#   - report/correctness json, flags_*.json, prompt/prompt_meta, summary
#     (json or txt), voided_reps txt, manifest_diff/runtime_source_manifest are
#     likewise already trackable via root .gitignore's `!**/results/**`
#     re-include plus the flags/report/correctness `!` rules above (both are
#     pattern-based, not job-prefix-based) — no new `!` rule was needed for
#     g2ctrl_*/g2ea_*/g2eaprobe_* to be tracked.
#   - No g2ctrl_*/g2ea_*/g2eaprobe_* srv log is cited by line number anywhere
#     in this repo as of 2026-08-08 (checked CONSENSUS.md, PROJECT_STATUS.md,
#     PREREG_G2EA_2026-08-07.md, PREREG_G2CTRL_2026-08-07.md) — same as
#     gate2's general rule, no exception carved back; add a narrow
#     `!results/p1_gates/gate2/<exact-file>.log` line if a future session
#     cites one by line number.
#   - flags_*.json volume re-checked for the larger E-A grid (5 arm x 10 rep x
#     2 rate): 146 files / 3.5MB for g2ea_*, 8 files / 192KB for g2ctrl_* —
#     still small enough to keep the existing "track all" policy (still the
#     only record of the realized-flag gate); no subsetting rule added.
# Net effect: no new `!`/exclude line below this comment — the existing
# extension/directory-scoped rules already generalize across job prefixes.

# g2det/g2detB (T4-1 determinism reconfirmation, jobs 876699/876766) and g2s
# (Gate 2-S, unsubmitted) raw-dump policy (2026-08-10), extending the 2026-08-
# 06/07/08 gate1/gate2/g2ctrl/E-A policy above to these two new naming
# families. Checked file-by-file against the untracked set (~230 files as of
# 2026-08-10) before writing anything below:
#   - g2det_*/g2detB_*: no *.jsonl, *.log, *.raw.json, or *_srv_*.log present
#     among the new files (verified) — everything else (summary/flags/
#     correctness-equivalent selfbaseline+raw json, prompt/prompt_meta,
#     nvidiasmi/procstate/pyspy diagnostic .txt snapshots, .status.json
#     measurement-failure sidecars, manifest_diff/runtime_source_manifest) is
#     small (<=24KB/file) and already trackable via root .gitignore's
#     `!**/results/**` re-include — no job-prefix-specific rule needed.
#     `*_selfbaseline_raw_*.json` looks like the excluded gate2 `*.raw.json`
#     class but is NOT the same thing and is NOT excluded: it does not match
#     the `*.raw.json` suffix pattern (the "raw" token is mid-filename, not a
#     `.raw.json` extension), and unlike the gate1/gate2 call1/call2 raw HTTP
#     bodies it is the ONLY record of that self-baseline response's
#     `meta_info.e2e_latency`, which g2_holb_phaseA_lib.sh's greedy_call
#     bounded-timeout comment cites in aggregate (n=64 across jobs) — kept
#     tracked deliberately, not by omission.
#   - g2s_*: only harness source (.py/.sbatch) present so far, no raw
#     artifacts exist yet (unsubmitted) — nothing to evaluate until it runs.
# Net effect: no new `!`/exclude line below this comment — the existing
# extension/directory-scoped rules already generalize across job prefixes.

# r0c dot-scratch (2026-08-11): .deckneectx2_* is the same P1.4-1.6-style
# runtime-scratch category as .nh_decode_sm_*/.p17mode_*/.la_chk_* above --
# a one-line context-length/round selector marker plus the degenerate
# repeated-text prompt body it points to, for job 873783's decode-context-
# length sweep. Not evidentiary: the scored output for that job
# (deckneectx2_result_C*_r1_873783.txt) is already tracked separately.
# .zb2smoke_*/ is the raw generation-comparison scratch dir for zb2smoke job
# 873617 (legacy-vs-patched greedy-decode text dumps + a copied patch
# source snapshot, used to eyeball a patch before scoring) -- its verdict
# (zb2smoke_result_873617.txt) is already tracked; the directory's contents
# are intermediate, same "harness+verdict tracked, raw not" convention as
# the gate2 rules above. Neither pattern deletes any file, only excludes
# from tracking; both were verified to match zero currently-tracked paths
# (`git ls-files | grep 'deckneectx2\|zb2smoke'` before this change listed
# only deckneectx2_result_*/runtime_source_manifest_deckneectx2v2.sha256/
# zb2smoke_result_873617.txt, none of which start with a dot).
.deckneectx2_*
.zb2smoke_*/

# gate2 smoke-harness raw prompts (2026-08-11): g2_holb_smoke.sbatch
# (tracked) is a pre-submission plumbing check only ("NO performance claim,
# no HOLB probe telemetry scored here" per its own header comment) run as
# jobs 874628/874631/874632. Its smoke_prompt_<tag>_<jobid>.txt prompt-body
# dumps were already excluded from tracking by explicit precedent -- see
# commit 7cf16bd's message: "smoke jobs 874628/874631/874632 are left out
# of this commit -- not part of this session's scope". This rule just makes
# `git status` reflect that existing decision instead of leaving the files
# perpetually untracked-but-visible; it does not delete anything and does
# not change the decision, only encodes it.
#
# Narrowed to *.txt only (2026-08-11, same-day follow-up): the original
# blanket `smoke_prompt_*` also matched smoke_prompt_meta_<tag>_<jobid>.json,
# which is now deliberately tracked (unlike the txt body) -- it is small
# (~250B) provenance (model/target_len/vocab_size/offset/reencoded_len/
# generator) that makes the ignored .txt prompt body reproducible, same
# "provenance kept, raw not" role the campaign-OUTPUTS convention plays
# elsewhere. Root .gitignore's **/results/**/smoke_prompt_*.txt (campaign
# runtime OUTPUTS section) now generalizes this pattern project-wide; this
# local line is redundant for gate2 specifically but kept, narrowed, for
# history.
results/p1_gates/gate2/smoke_prompt_*.txt
results/s8_scaleup/.s0a_cells_cache.pkl
